1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The world saw — a river, a
road, a seam.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,000
To the Chinese, the Milky Way was a
river: Tianhe, “the Heavenly River.”

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Along it they placed star pools, a boat,
a ford, and another river.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The ancient text Erya puts the river’s
ford between Ji (“Winnowing Basket”) and
Dou (“Southern Dipper”).

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,000
In ancient Arabia, Ji’s four stars were
ostriches going to drink. Four in Dou
were heading back after drinking.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Others saw a road for souls, a seam, a
dragon, even ash.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
It is our own galaxy: a disc about
100,000 light-years wide.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:12,000
On northern summer nights we face the
galaxy’s centre — in Sagittarius, right
by that ford, 27,000 light-years away.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:19,000
On a moonless night, get far from city
lights. Late evening, look low in the
south.

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Season finale: many ways of seeing one
sky.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

